<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Norici</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Norici were a Celtic people of the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>, in what is now <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carinthia">Carinthia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. In the 2nd century BCE they led a union of tribes that formed the kingdom of Noricum, which traded its famous iron with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. After Noricum was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> around 16 BCE, the name survived as that of the Roman province.</p></div>
